Make __builtin_signbit type generic (backport for Clang 3.4)

Clang 3.4 declares __builtin_signbit as int(double), so Sema promotes a float
argument to double and demotes a long double one, before CodeGen ever sees it.
glibc >= 2.32 defines signbit(x) as __builtin_signbit(x) for Clang >= 3.3, so
every signbit() call on a non-double goes through that conversion.

Under KLEE's SMT-LIB floating point semantics the conversion is not harmless:
fpext of a NaN yields the canonical NaN, which has no sign, so signbit() of a
negative NaN wrongly answers 0 and KLEE loses that path entirely.

CGBuiltin.cpp already emits a width-generic bitcast+icmp, and
SemaBuiltinFPClassification() already strips the float->double cast, so it is
enough to declare the builtin with custom type checking like its __builtin_isnan
siblings. This is the same fix LLVM made upstream after 3.4.

--- a/tools/clang/include/clang/Basic/Builtins.def
+++ b/tools/clang/include/clang/Basic/Builtins.def
@@ -371,7 +371,7 @@
 BUILTIN(__builtin_isnormal,   "i.", "nc")
 
 // FP signbit builtins
-BUILTIN(__builtin_signbit, "id", "nc")
+BUILTIN(__builtin_signbit, "i.", "nc")
 BUILTIN(__builtin_signbitf, "if", "nc")
 BUILTIN(__builtin_signbitl, "iLd", "nc")
 
--- a/tools/clang/lib/Sema/SemaChecking.cpp
+++ b/tools/clang/lib/Sema/SemaChecking.cpp
@@ -163,6 +163,7 @@
   case Builtin::BI__builtin_isinf_sign:
   case Builtin::BI__builtin_isnan:
   case Builtin::BI__builtin_isnormal:
+  case Builtin::BI__builtin_signbit:
     if (SemaBuiltinFPClassification(TheCall, 1))
       return ExprError();
     break;
